<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n93257" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σᾱπέρδ-ης</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>the fish</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κορακῖνος</span>, prob. the <i>great
				Nile-perch, Tilapia nilotica</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>Int.</u>
				25
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Frr.</u>
				414
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				686
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Archipp.
				26
			</span></i>; a Pontic fish acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Archestr.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				38.3
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς. τῶν ἐκ τῆς λίμνης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>PCair.Zen.</u>
					680.33
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii B.C.)</span>; found in the Maeander, <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Abst.</u>
				3.5
			</span></i>; both the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κορακῖνος</span> and the
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πλατίστακος</span> were called <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ς</span>. acc. to <i><span class="en">
				Parmeno
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				7.308f
			</span></i>; cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σαπερδίς</span>.</div>
